From ea0622bc4a3a2acada488574cf4bd83b297a6c68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max Lv <max.c.lv@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 15:22:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] termio: add passthru IO backend for embedder-provided IO
 (SSH)

Add a new `passthru` termio backend that owns no subprocess or pty.
Instead, the embedder provides IO:

  * Incoming data is injected via the new C API ghostty_surface_pty_data,
    which feeds Termio.processOutput (the same ingress the exec backend's
    read thread uses).
  * Outgoing data (keyboard input, query responses, etc.) flows through
    the single queueWrite chokepoint to an embedder-provided callback.
  * Resizes are reported via a callback so the embedder can notify the
    remote (e.g. an SSH window-change request).

The backend is selected via a new `io_backend` field on
ghostty_surface_config_s, with pty_write_cb / pty_resize_cb callbacks.
Surface.init branches on the apprt's ioBackend()/passthruConfig()
(detected at comptime so only the embedded/libghostty apprt is affected)
to skip subprocess creation.

This enables driving libghostty from a network transport such as SSH,
e.g. on iOS where fork/exec is unavailable. Used by the gterm iOS app.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
